    "created_at": "2018-02-21T19:26:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-21T19:26:53Z",
    "body": "> I think we should also remove the step starting with \"If the user agent has already reached the last step of this list of steps\" since that doesn't seem possible to happen?\r\n\r\nNo, I think this happens in cases like\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<input autofocus>\r\n<input autofocus>\r\n```\r\n\r\nEncountering the first one queues a task that goes all the way through to the end. Encountering the second one queues a task that hits that step and then returns.\r\n\r\nInterestingly, per https://output.jsbin.com/daviyegepu/1 this flag appears to be set forever (like the current spec says); it doesn't, for example, reset when the task completes.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
